SUMMARY:Women in Machine Learning and Data Science
DTSTAMP:20260915T174748Z
DTSTART:20251124T220000Z
DTEND:20251125T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive workshop\, where we will explore adv
	anced techniques in the field of AI and machine learning. This event is op
	en to all skill levels\, from beginners to experienced data scientists\, i
	nterested in expanding their knowledge and practical skills.\n\nWHEN: Mond
	ay\, Nov 24th\, 6-8pm\nLOCATION: VOLTA.\n\nSpeaker Lineup (5 min presentat
	ions\, 10 mins Q&A):\n\nTBD..\n\nHuge thank you to them for providing spac
	e for us to connect in-person.\nIf you're interested in sharing your own t
	ools\, tricks and ideas\, please fill this out and we can add to to the up
	coming or a future session.\nhttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd3J
	O3i9WIo2uFxKIxTeAi577Iu2nC_ounBYFZxTzYbxKfxSQ/viewform?usp=dialog\n\nAt Wi
	MLDS Halifax\, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive commu
	nity of women in Machine Learning and Data Science. Come network with like
	-minded individuals\, share your experiences\, and engage in stimulating d
	iscussions around data analytics\, predictive analytics\, and more. Whethe
	r you are a seasoned professional or just starting out in the field\, this
	 workshop is a great opportunity to learn\, grow\, and connect with other 
	women in tech.
URL:https://www.meetup.com/halifax-women-in-machine-learning-and-data-scien
	ce/events/311889285/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:community
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jibmvKKRKnLb4P0L5y04q
SUMMARY:AI Mixer and Showcase Sydney
DTSTAMP:20260915T174748Z
DTSTART:20251125T200000Z
DTEND:20251125T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Explore AI & connect with innovators in Sydney. Join Volta & IG
	NITE for an evening of networking and ideas! With guest speaker Wayne Mill
	er!\nArtificial Intelligence is transforming industries—and it’s happening
	 right here in Nova Scotia. Join Volta and IGNITE for the AI Mixer in Sydn
	ey\, an evening designed to connect curious minds\, tech professionals\, a
	nd innovators.\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat to Expect:\n\n✔ Engaging Conversations – Le
	arn how AI is being applied locally and globally.\n\n✔ Networking Opportun
	ities – Meet entrepreneurs\, tech experts\, and AI enthusiasts.\n\n✔ Commu
	nity Building – Be part of Nova Scotia’s growing innovation ecosystem.\n\n
	\n\n\n\n📅 Date: Tuesday\, November 25th\n\n🕓 Time: 4:00 PM – 6:00 PM\n\n📍 
	Location: Fired Creations\, Sydney\, NS\n\n\n\n\n\nWhether you’re new to A
	I or already exploring its potential\, this event is your chance to learn\
	, connect\, and collaborate.\n\n____________________________\n\nWayne Mill
	er is a Cape Breton–based entrepreneur recognized by many as “the smoothie
	 guy” from his time running Downtown Nutrition\, a local health and smooth
	ie shop that became a community staple. Following the pandemic\, Wayne tra
	nsitioned into the tech space as part of Digital Nova Scotia’s first SaaS 
	Tech Sales cohort\, later joining 45Drives\, where he championed the launc
	h of their new division\, 45Professional.\n\nEager to continue his journey
	 in tech\, Wayne connected with Volta and its vision to bridge the gap bet
	ween local business and technology — a natural fit for his entrepreneurial
	 mindset. While exploring coding\, no-code tools\, and AI\, one insight fr
	om a Volta Vibe Coding session stuck with him: “Your perspective\, your in
	sight\, and your lived experience are the foundation of innovation.” That 
	sparked the creation of BrainThrive\, a project inspired by challenges in 
	his own family life — transforming a personal problem into a purpose-drive
	n solution.\n\nBrainThrive is a gamified screen-time management app design
	ed for kids and parents. It turns healthy digital habits into a fun challe
	nge where kids earn rewards for balanced screen use and task completion\, 
	while parents get tools to monitor and encourage positive behavior. The go
	al: transform screen-time struggles into opportunities for growth and conn
	ection.
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/ai-mixer-showcase-sydney-tickets-1969384040
	680?aff=ebemoffollowpublishemail&ref=eemail&utm_campaign=following_publish
	ed_event&utm_content=follow_notification&utm_medium=email&utm_source=event
	brite
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:community
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aoKQE0cx5v5hKXiUzaw8m
SUMMARY:Crypto\, Blockchain\, AI\, and the Changing Landscape of Financial 
	Markets
DTSTAMP:20260915T174748Z
DTSTART:20251126T180000Z
DTEND:20251126T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Between crypto rebounds\, AI breakthroughs\, and shifting marke
	t moods\, 2025 has been full of noise. This session takes a step back to s
	ee what’s actually happening underneath it all. We’ll start with the found
	ations: what makes Bitcoin work\, how blockchain builds trust through dece
	ntralization and cryptography\, and what’s new in crypto\, including stabl
	ecoins\, tokenization\, institutional investment\, and regulation reshapin
	g the space.\n\nThen we’ll zoom out to how AI is transforming finance and 
	where these two worlds are beginning to overlap. Using recent market data 
	and investor sentiment\, the talk connects the dots between technology\, c
	apital flows\, and behaviour\, uncovering where innovation is emerging and
	 how markets are responding to it.\n\n\n\n6:00PM – 6:15PM: Welcome & Regis
	tration\n\n6:15PM – 6:20PM: Sponsor Speech\n\n6:20PM – 7:00PM: Presentatio
	n\n\n7:00PM – 7:45PM: Networking\n\n7:45PM – 8:00PM: Program End
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/crypto-blockchain-ai-and-the-changing-lands
	cape-of-financial-markets-tickets-1946072819189
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:community
END:VEVENT
