BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:AyWdNi1-CiMy_mnDBGlsI
SUMMARY:Education in the Age of AI: Turning the "Why?" into an Interactive 
	Learning Adventure
DTSTAMP:20260915T174748Z
DTSTART:20260128T220000Z
DTEND:20260129T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><strong>Speaker: </strong><a target="_blank" rel="nofollow n
	oopener noreferrer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/yuhan-fu-079ab3182/"
	><strong><u>Yuhan Fu | LinkedIn</u></strong></a></p><p>Every child goes th
	rough the "Why?" phase. It is the spark of learning\, but it can be overwh
	elming for the adults trying to keep the flame alive. With the rapid and t
	ransformative growth of AI\, we are now presented with new possibilities t
	o support\, guide\, and amplify this natural curiosity in ways that were n
	ot possible before.</p><p>This session will share a personal exploration i
	nto the future of learning. Rather than just offering quick answers\, my p
	roject explores how AI can help turn a child’s curiosity into an interacti
	ve learning journey. Join us to discuss the potential of AI-assisted educa
	tion and see where this experiment leads.</p><p><br></p><p>6:00PM – 6:15PM
	: Welcome &amp\; Registration</p><p>6:15PM – 6:20PM: Sponsor Speech</p><p>
	6:20PM – 7:00PM: Presentation</p><p>7:00PM – 7:45PM: Networking</p><p>7:45
	PM – 8:00PM: Program End</p>
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/education-in-the-age-of-ai-tickets-19796308
	98307
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:community
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikJeDo31iNuc7xr5esLiW
SUMMARY:Building with ML: Meetup & Shares
DTSTAMP:20260915T174748Z
DTSTART:20260204T210000Z
DTEND:20260204T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Hosted: RED space</p><p></p><p>We’ve been hosting internal B
	uilding with ML meetups here at REDspace and they’ve been too good not to 
	share with everyone.<br><br>So we’re inviting folks from the tech communit
	y to join us for a FREE fundamentals-first\, discussion-driven Machine Lea
	rning meetup. No conference talks or pitch decks\, this is real conversati
	ons about building these systems\, observing their behaviour\, and learnin
	g the art of building them.<br><br>Expect:<br>• Open discussion\, demos\, 
	and problem-solving<br>• Core concepts and practical techniques<br>• All e
	xperience levels welcome<br>• Lots of curiosity and shared learning<br><br
	>Bring something to share\; a technique you tried\, a model behaviour you 
	noticed\, a paper you found interesting\, or a project you’re working on. 
	It’s open to the public\, all are welcome!<br><br>Sign-in: 5:00pm – 5:30pm
	</p>
URL:https://luma.com/45yy66ea
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:community
END:VEVENT
