DESCRIPTION:<p>Join the ONSIDE + Campus2Market Discover Program!</p><p></p>
	<p><strong>ONSIDE</strong>\, in collaboration with <strong>Dal Innovates</
	strong>\, is proud to deliver <strong>Campus2Market Discover</strong>\, a 
	unique program designed for women and underserved entrepreneurs across Atl
	antic Canada.</p><p></p><p>This is not your typical workshop — it’s an imm
	ersive experience where ideas meet action. Over three days\, you’ll explor
	e the fundamentals of building a venture\, from identifying real-world pro
	blems to crafting a compelling pitch. Learn\, collaborate\, and innovate a
	longside a community of forward-thinking entrepreneurs.</p><p></p><p>You m
	ust be in Halifax for the duration of this program\, as 2/3 of the days wi
	ll be in-person.</p><p></p><p><strong>Schedule</strong></p><p><strong>Frid
	ay\, March 13 | 12:00–1:30 PM (Online via Zoom)</strong></p><ul><li><p><st
	rong>Kickoff:</strong> introductions\, program overview\, and networking</
	p></li><li><p></p></li></ul><p><strong>Saturday\, March 14 | 9:30 AM–4:30 
	PM (In Person)</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>- Design Thinking &amp\; Pro
	blem Framing:</strong> develop empathy for your users and define meaningfu
	l\, impactful problems.</p></li><li><p><strong>- Business Model Canvas:</s
	trong> map out your solution\, target audience\, and business strategy wit
	h Bernice Williams\, the Founder of Intentional Connection!</p></li><li><p
	><strong>Customer Discovery:</strong> conduct interviews and validate your
	 idea with real users</p></li><li><p></p></li></ul><p><strong>Sunday\, Mar
	ch 15 | 9:30 AM–3:00 PM (In Person)</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>- Pitch
	 Development:</strong> craft your story and communicate your idea with cla
	rity and confidence. Receive expert guidance from Rashmi Prakash - Founder
	 of Aruna Revolution\, who has been on Dragon's Den!</p></li><li><p><stron
	g>- Pitch Practice &amp\; Working Session:</strong> refine your presentati
	on with expert feedback</p></li><li><p><strong>- Final Pitch Session &amp\
	; Next Steps:</strong> present your 1–2 minute pitch\, compete for cash pr
	izes\, and explore opportunities within the entrepreneurial ecosystem.</p>
	</li><li><p></p></li></ul><p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p><ul><li><p>- 
	Graduates from the past five years of an Atlantic Canada university or col
	lege</p></li><li><p>- Current post-secondary students (Undergrad\, Master’
	s\, or PhD)</p></li><li><p></p></li></ul><p><strong>Who Will Benefit Most?
	</strong></p><ul><li><p>- Early-stage entrepreneurs ready to grow their id
	eas</p></li><li><p>- People who are currently working on their undergradua
	te degree or have graduated in the last 5 years from any university level 
	(Bachelor's\, Undergrad\, PhD\, etc.)</p></li><li><p>- Individuals with a 
	business idea they haven’t launched yet</p></li><li><p>- Founders with ini
	tial customers seeking structure\, strategy\, and growth</p></li><li><p></
	p></li></ul><p><strong>Why Join?</strong></p><ul><li><p>- Gain hands-on ex
	perience in innovation and entrepreneurship</p></li><li><p>- Test and de-r
	isk your business idea before launching</p></li><li><p>- Learn the skills 
	and mindset needed to turn ideas into impact</p></li><li><p>- Expand your 
	network with current and future entrepreneurs</p></li><li><p>- Compete in 
