UID:4ukI3_vSbp7QS7LLMzROk
SUMMARY:Humans In AI: East Coast Kitchen Party
DTSTAMP:20260915T174748Z
DTSTART:20260602T203000Z
DTEND:20260602T234900Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>​<strong>200</strong>+ cities<strong>. 50+ </strong>countrie
	s<strong>. One week. One question.</strong></p><p><strong>​What does it me
	an to be human in the AI era?</strong></p><p>​It's <a target="_blank" rel=
	"nofollow noopener" href="https://www.humansinaiweek.com/?utm_source=luma"
	><strong>Humans in AI Week</strong></a><strong>\,</strong> the largest coo
	rdinated civilian conversation about AI ever organized and Halifax is in i
	t.</p><p>​We're answering it the Nova Scotia way: live fiddler\, East Coas
	t food and drinks\, and the people actually building AI for real people in
	 this city.</p><p>​Haligonians building with AI take the mic to answer one
	 question directly: <strong><em>what are you building\, and how does it im
	pact the humans in this city?</em> </strong>The room talks back after ever
	yone.</p><p>​✨ <strong>Who's in the room:</strong></p><ul><li><p>​AI build
	ers and founders shaping Halifax's AI economy</p></li><li><p>​Policy\, bus
	iness\, and community leaders navigating what AI means for their sector</p
	></li><li><p>​The people deciding what gets built and who it's built for</
