SUMMARY:Patent 102: Building and Protecting IP for Life Science Startups
DTSTAMP:20260915T174748Z
DTSTART:20260716T170000Z
DTEND:20260716T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>An in-person &amp\; virtual session hosted by Springboard At
	lantic\, Life Sciences Nova Scotia</p><p>Intellectual property is one of t
	he most valuable assets for an early-stage company—but knowing how to prot
	ect and leverage it effectively is critical.</p><p></p><p>Join us for <str
	ong>Patent 102</strong>\, an informative session designed for early-stage 
	companies\, with a particular focus on the life sciences sector. This pres
	entation will explore key intellectual property considerations that can im
	pact growth\, investment readiness\, and long-term success.</p><p></p><p>T
	opics will include:</p><ul><li><p>Common IP pitfalls and how to avoid them
	</p></li><li><p>Patents versus trade secrets: understanding the difference
	s</p></li><li><p>Building and managing a patent portfolio to maximize comp
	any valuation</p></li><li><p>Strategic IP considerations for startups and 
	growing companies</p></li><li><p>Real-world case studies from Canadian com
	panies</p></li><li><p></p></li></ul><p><strong>Speaker: Steven Lam\, Paten
	t Agent\, ROBIC</strong></p><p>Steven Lam is the Practice Group Leader of 
	ROBIC's Chemistry and Life Sciences (ChemLife) Patent Group. With more tha
	n 20 years of experience as a patent professional and a background in bioc
	hemistry\, he helps Canadian and international clients protect\, manage\, 
	and commercialize intellectual property.</p><p></p><p>Steven specializes i
	n patent drafting and prosecution in Canada\, the United States\, and inte
	rnationally\, and advises on patentability\, validity\, infringement\, and
	 freedom-to-operate matters. He works with companies of all sizes\, partic
	ularly in biotechnology and life sciences\, including pharmaceuticals\, di
	agnostics\, genome editing\, immunology\, and agricultural biotechnology.<
	/p>
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/patent-102-building-and-protecting-ip-for-l
	ife-science-startups-tickets-1991388261898?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:community
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
