	rnate routes to Volta. For the easiest access, we recommend using <strong>
	<strong>Entrance 2 (2nd Floor Arch Entrance)</strong></strong> or <strong>
	<strong>Entrance 3 (Argyle Street Link Entrance)</strong></strong>.</p><p>
	<br></p><p><strong><strong>Description:</strong></strong></p><p>This sessi
	on, hosted by <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sam-eugene-silver/" tit
	le="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sam-eugene-silver/" target="_blank" data-m
	sys-clicktrack="0" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"><strong><strong>Sam 
	Silver</strong></strong></a>, features special guest <a href="https://www.
	linkedin.com/in/darrylwright/" title="https://www.linkedin.com/in/darrylwr
	ight/" target="_blank" data-msys-clicktrack="0" rel="nofollow noopener nor
	eferrer"><strong><strong>Darryl Wright</strong></strong></a> for a hands-o
	n look at game development through the lens of disciplined AI workflows.</
	p><p>Darryl will kick things off with the building blocks of game developm
	ent, from game loops and events to input and rendering, before diving into
	 the real challenge: moving beyond one-shot vibe coding to architecting co
	mplete game systems with AI harnesses.</p><p>And then comes the fun part: 
	we'll put it all into practice by building a modern 3D arcade game live, f
	rom start to finish, in just a few minutes.</p><p>Whether you're intereste
	d in game development, AI-assisted coding, or how more structured AI workf
	lows can help you build better software, this session will offer a practic
	al and entertaining look at what's possible when the two come together.</p
	></div><div style="margin: 20px 0;line-height: 22px;"><img src="https://im
	g.evbuc.com/https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.evbuc.com%2Fimages%2F1191333569%2F5700208188
