UID:WJN59ENVOQvUAP_WvGs3n
SUMMARY:Yoga
DTSTAMP:20260915T174749Z
DTSTART:20260924T104500Z
DTEND:20260924T114500Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a 1-hour guided yoga session designed specifically 
	for busy\, desk-based lifestyles.
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/yoga-tickets-1996833913990
LOCATION:Volta
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:eventbrite
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div>Join us for a 1-hour guided yoga session 
	designed specifically for busy, desk-based lifestyles.</div><div style="ma
	rgin-top: 20px"><div style="margin: 20px 10px;font-size: 15px;line-height:
	 22px;font-weight: 400;text-align: left;"><p><strong><strong>When:</strong
	></strong><strong><strong> </strong></strong>August 20, September 10 and 2
	4, 2026 (register for each date individually) from 7:45am - 8:45am</p><p><
	strong><strong>Where:</strong></strong><strong><strong> </strong></strong>
	Volta, 1800 Argyle St., Unit 801, Halifax, NS, B3J 3N8</p><p><strong><stro
	ng>Please note:</strong></strong> The Armoyan Centre's main entrance is cu
	rrently closed due to construction. <a href="https://drive.google.com/file
	/d/1HaQDEMlyDSpYttrarfJePVOlx38Kqzer/view" title="https://drive.google.com
	/file/d/1HaQDEMlyDSpYttrarfJePVOlx38Kqzer/view" target="_blank" data-msys-
	clicktrack="0" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">Please review the access
	 guide</a> for alternate routes to Volta. For the easiest access, we recom
	mend using <strong><strong>Entrance 2 (2nd Floor Arch Entrance)</strong></
	strong> or <strong><strong>Entrance 3 (Argyle Street Link Entrance)</stron
	g></strong>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Bring your own mat</strong><
	/strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Description:</strong></strong></
	p><p>Join us for a 1-hour guided yoga session designed specifically for bu
	sy, desk-based lifestyles. Rooted in traditional Ashtanga yoga principles,
	 these sessions offer a structured yet accessible practice focused on impr
	oving posture, building strength, and relieving tension in the neck and sh
	oulders.</p><p>Each session includes 45 minutes of intentional movement—le
	arning how to properly engage and release muscles in each pose—followed by
	 15 minutes of calming breathwork to reduce stress, enhance focus, and sup
	port overall well-being.</p><p>Perfect for anyone looking to move better, 
	feel better, and bring more balance and clarity into their workday.</p><p>
	<br></p><p><strong><strong>Your Practitioner:</strong></strong><strong><st
	rong> </strong></strong>Jaimee Lee - Baggley</p><p><br></p></div><div styl
	e="margin: 20px 0;line-height: 22px;"><img src="https://img.evbuc.com/http
	s%3A%2F%2Fcdn.evbuc.com%2Fimages%2F1190402843%2F57002081887%2F1%2Foriginal
	.20260805-193121?h=740&w=1200&auto=format%2Ccompress&q=75&sharp=10&s=150a5
	492992f0a15172e60ef0f04ab73" alt="" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto" 
	/></div><div style="margin: 20px 10px;font-size: 15px;line-height: 22px;fo
	nt-weight: 400;text-align: left;"><p>With a yoga teacher certification and
	 over 24 years of personal practice, Jaimee specializes in delivering acce
	ssible, workplace-appropriate yoga and mindfulness programs. She teaches t
	he Ashtanga Standing and Primary Series with a strong emphasis on breath, 
	stability, and functional movement, adapting practices through the use of 
	props so participants can safely engage at their own pace. Her work is sup
	ported by a consistent daily practice and regular pranayama, contributing 
	to a steady, grounded presence that participants consistently report as ca
	lming and confidence-building.</p><p>Jaimee is an experienced yoga and min
	dfulness practitioner with more than two decades of dedicated practice gro
	unded in traditional Hatha and Ashtanga yoga. Her training reflects a deep
	 commitment to lineage-based learning and includes direct, in-person study
	 with senior teachers Manju Jois and Sathu Jois, as well as ongoing mentor
	ship with authorized instructors Greg Tebb and Andrea Gracia. She has been
	 granted permission from Greg Tebb, apprentice of Manju Jois, to teach thi
	s specialized yoga. This foundation informs a teaching approach that is di
	sciplined, precise, and respectful of individual capacity.</p><p>Jaimee ha
	s experience delivering both group and individualized sessions in professi
	onal environments, including corporate wellness programming, on-site class
	es, and one-to-one therapeutic sessions. Her facilitation style is clear, 
	structured, and responsive to the realities of modern workplaces, supporti
	ng mobility, stress recovery, nervous system regulation, and sustained foc
	us.</p><p><br></p></div></div>
END:VEVENT
