BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:QZyEkjlpRotUczHP8T0Wl
SUMMARY:Turning Cybersecurity\, Privacy and AI Governance into a Business A
	dvantage
DTSTAMP:20260915T174749Z
DTSTART:20260928T150000Z
DTEND:20260928T163000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Darren Gallop for Built to Trust: Turning Cybersecurity\, 
	Privacy and AI Governance into a Business Advantage!
URL:https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/turning-cybersecurity-privacy-and-ai-govern
	ance-into-a-business-advantage-tickets-1998983989925
LOCATION:Volta
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:eventbrite
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div>Join Darren Gallop for Built to Trust: Tu
	rning Cybersecurity, Privacy and AI Governance into a Business Advantage!<
	/div><div style="margin-top: 20px"><div style="margin: 20px 10px;font-size
	: 15px;line-height: 22px;font-weight: 400;text-align: left;"><p><strong><s
	trong>When: </strong></strong>Monday, September 28, 2026 from 12:00pm - 1:
	30pm</p><p><strong><strong>Where: </strong></strong>Volta, 1800 Argyle St.
	, Unit 801, Halifax, NS, B3J 3N8</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Please n
	ote:</strong></strong> The Armoyan Centre's main entrance is currently clo
	sed due to construction. <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HaQDEMl
	yDSpYttrarfJePVOlx38Kqzer/view" title="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ha
	QDEMlyDSpYttrarfJePVOlx38Kqzer/view" target="_blank" data-msys-clicktrack=
	"0" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">Please review the access guide</a> 
	for alternate routes to Volta. For the easiest access, we recommend using 
	<strong><strong>Entrance 2 (2nd Floor Arch Entrance)</strong></strong> or 
	<strong><strong>Entrance 3 (Argyle Street Link Entrance)</strong></strong>
	.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Description:</strong></strong></p><p>As
	 organizations race to adopt AI and increasingly depend on data and techno
	logy, cybersecurity, privacy and governance can no longer be treated simpl
	y as technical or compliance problems.</p><p>In this practical, business-f
	ocused session, Darren will explore the concept of <strong><strong>Trust C
	apital</strong></strong> and how founders and business leaders can deliber
	ately build trust into their organizations without creating unnecessary bu
	reaucracy or slowing innovation. He’ll look at how companies can balance t
	he need to move quickly, particularly with AI, against the very real secur
	ity, privacy and governance risks that come with it.</p><p>Drawing on more
	 than two decades of experience building technology companies, Darren will
	 share practical lessons, real-world stories and a straightforward approac
	h to building organizations that customers, partners, employees and invest
	ors can trust.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p></div><div style="margin: 20px 0;l
	ine-height: 22px;"><img src="https://img.evbuc.com/https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.evbuc
	.com%2Fimages%2F1191967854%2F57002081887%2F1%2Foriginal.20260826-181319?h=
	740&w=1200&auto=format%2Ccompress&q=75&sharp=10&s=f548933d97c84bc2cd42c267
	8aa1d315" alt="" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto" /></div><div style=
